    "title": "UConn's Braylon Mullins not related to NBA legend Chris Mullin - Greenfield Today",
    "text": "Mar. 27, 2026 at 8:40am Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›Braylon Mullins, a freshman guard for the UConn Huskies, has emerged as a key contributor this season. With his last name resembling that of NBA Hall of Famer Chris Mullin, some have wondered if the two are related. However, it has been confirmed that Braylon Mullins and Chris Mullin are not actually related, despite their shared basketball background. Why it matters The similarity in last names between Braylon Mullins and Chris Mullin has led to some confusion and speculation about a potential family connection between the two basketball players. Clarifying that they are not actually related helps provide accurate information to fans and media following Braylon Mullins' promising freshman season at UConn. The details Braylon Mullins is a 19-year-old freshman guard at the University of Connecticut, listed at 6-foot-6 and 196 pounds. He has been a key contributor for the Huskies this season, averaging 12.1 points, 3.5 rebounds and 1.5 assists per game. Mullins was a consensus top-25 recruit in the 2025 class and is considered a potential NBA draft pick. While Mullins' last name may sound familiar to basketball fans due to its similarity to Chris Mullin, the former NBA All-Star and Hall of Famer, the two are not actually related. Braylon's father, Josh Mullins, played college basketball but is not connected to Chris Mullin's family. Braylon Mullins is a freshman at UConn during the 2025-26 season. The players Braylon MullinsA 19-year-old freshman guard for the UConn Huskies, Braylon Mullins has emerged as a key contributor this season, averaging 12.1 points, 3.5 rebounds and 1.5 assists per game.Chris MullinA Basketball Hall of Famer and five-time NBA All-Star, Chris Mullin is a legendary basketball player, but he is not related to UConn's Braylon Mullins despite the similarity in their last names.Josh MullinsBraylon Mullins' father, Josh Mullins, played college basketball at Lincoln Trail College and Indiana University–Purdue University Indianapolis (IUPUI). Got photos? Submit your photos here. › The takeaway While the last names of Braylon Mullins and Chris Mullin may sound similar, the two basketball players are not actually related. Braylon Mullins is making a name for himself as a promising freshman at UConn, and his family basketball background comes from his father, Josh Mullins, not the NBA legend Chris Mullin.",
